	<!--
		v300 - UI Button + web view instead of Thermostat + Extras
		=========================================================
		The thermostatV2 proxy (v200-v204) made the shower look like a second
		thermostat in the room and put its temperature in the room header.
		Rooms with a real HVAC thermostat need the shower to sit NEXT to it,
		so the shower is now a uibutton proxy whose tile opens a custom page
		(www/shower2.html) in Navigator: temperature ring, start/stop, preset
		tiles, temp stepper and outlet toggles.

		PACKAGE NAME: moenshower.c4z, and <name> is the same slug. Navigator
		resolves controller://driver/moenshower/... from it; if the two do
		not match, Navigator hides the tile. Changing proxy type means this
		must be ADDED as a new device (delete the v20x device first) - so the
		old Moen_Smart_Shower_Standalone_driver_v200 package name is retired
		here, and every build after this keeps moenshower.c4z.

		PAGE FILE IS RENAMED EVERY PAGE RELEASE (shower1, shower2, ...)
		because Navigator caches controller:// pages. web_view_url below,
		PAGE_FILE / PAGE_BUILD in the Lua and the file in www/ must agree.

		Protocol layer (REST auth, polling, Pusher websocket, Action_*
		payloads) is unchanged from v204.
	-->
	<!--
		v302 - Local Bridge transport (default) or Moen Cloud, as in the
		standalone driver v206. Bridge = JSON lines over TCP, port 8765, on
		dynamic binding 7001. Page renamed to shower2.html.
	-->
	<proxies qty="1">
		<proxy proxybindingid="5001" name="Shower" primary="True" image_source="c4z" small_image="icons/device_sm.png" large_image="icons/device_lg.png">uibutton</proxy>
	</proxies>

